// Sims1Pkg's interface text, in English. Other languages lay their own
// _100_sims1pkg.cst over this one, in uitext/<language>.dir, and any value
// they leave out or leave empty falls back to this table. %s and %d are
// filled in by the app.

// The window
app title ^Sims1Pkg^
window minimize ^Minimize^
window maximize ^Maximize^
window restore ^Restore^
window close ^Close^

// The sidebar
sidebar installed ^Installed (%d)^
sidebar open ^Open package…^
sidebar new ^New package…^
sidebar game label ^Installing into:^
sidebar no game ^Choose the game folder…^

// A package before installing
package author ^by %s^
package version ^version %s^
package id ^id %s^
package unknown kinds ^This package has files this version of Sims1Pkg doesn't know how to install. A newer Sims1Pkg may be able to install it.^
frame contents ^Contents^
column file ^File^
column kind ^Kind^
column destination ^Goes to^
kind object ^Object^
kind skin ^Skin^
kind wall ^Wall^
kind floor ^Floor^
kind unknown ^Unknown (%s)^
destination unknown ^Can't be installed^
button install ^Install^
button update ^Update^
button reinstall ^Reinstall^
button cancel ^Cancel^

// Installing
installing ^Installing %s…^
summary installed ^%s is installed.^
summary hint ^Start The Sims to see it. Uninstall it from Installed at any time.^
button done ^Done^

// Installed packages
installed title ^Installed packages^
installed empty ^Nothing is installed yet. Open a package to install it.^
installed problems ^Some install records couldn't be read:^
installed on ^Installed %s^
installed replaced ^Replaced a file that's put back on uninstall^
button uninstall ^Uninstall^
uninstalled ^%s is uninstalled.^

// Making a package
pack title ^New package^
pack intro ^Choose the folder that holds the content. Files in Downloads, GameData/Skins, GameData/Walls, or GameData/Floors folders go there in the game. Other files are placed by their type.^
pack choose folder ^Choose folder…^
pack folder ^Folder: %s^
pack empty ^There's nothing to pack in this folder.^
pack left out ^Left out: %s^
frame details ^Details^
field name ^Name^
field author ^Author^
field date ^Date (YYYY-MM-DD)^
field id ^Id (optional, keep it the same for every version)^
field version ^Version^
field description ^Description^
field license ^License^
field source url ^Web page^
problem name missing ^Give the package a name.^
problem author missing ^Say who made it.^
problem date ^Write the date as YYYY-MM-DD.^
problem id not valid ^An id uses letters, numbers, dots, dashes, and underscores, up to 64.^
problem source url ^The web page must start with http:// or https://.^
problem no kind ^Can't tell what this is^
problem path not valid ^Name Windows doesn't allow^
problem name clash ^Clashes with another file^
button save package ^Save package…^
pack saved ^Saved %s.^

// Popups
clash title ^Some files are already in your game^
clash message ^%s wants to replace these files. Your copies will be kept, so uninstalling puts them back.^
button replace ^Replace^
update title ^Update %s?^
update message ^Version %s is installed. Install version %s in its place?^
no version ^(none)^
reinstall title ^Install %s again?^
reinstall message ^This version is already installed. Install it again?^
uninstall title ^Uninstall %s?^
uninstall message ^This removes everything it installed and puts back any files it replaced.^
uninstall changed ^These files were changed since they were installed, and will be removed too:^
uninstall missing ^These files are already gone:^
game title ^Where is The Sims?^
game message ^Choose the folder The Sims is installed in. It holds the GameData and UserData folders.^
game not a game ^That folder doesn't look like The Sims. It should hold GameData and UserData folders.^
no game ^Choose the game folder first.^
admin title ^Administrator rights needed^
admin message ^The game is in a folder Windows protects. Sims1Pkg will ask for administrator rights to install into it.^
button continue ^Continue^
not writable ^Sims1Pkg can't write to %s. Check that you're allowed to change files there.^
error title ^Something went wrong^
open failed ^%s couldn't be opened.^
button ok ^OK^

// File pickers
picker packages ^Sims1Pkg packages^
picker open title ^Open package^
picker save title ^Save package^
picker folder title ^Choose a folder^
